{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492104-some-thoughts-and-questions-about-low-humanity","id":1492104,"title":"Some thoughts and questions about low Humanity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-01T11:49:19-07:00","id":1492104,"title":"Some thoughts and questions about low Humanity","content":"I've been watching a lot of vampire media lately and one specific thing that I've noticed is that in a lot of those stories vampire's appearance is directly tied to their state of mind. And, considering how it tends to degrade with the passage of time, directly tied with age. So I began to ponder about the similar ideas in VtR. Considering how vampire's struggle with the Beast is represented by Humanity scale, I asked myself: Do vampires with low Humanity look any different from their regular brethren? And if so, does it (or should it) impose any tangible disadvantages on their interactions with mortals? I'd really like to hear your thoughts on the matter.<br /> <br /> The Corebook for 2E mentions that as the Beast takes more control, kindred's body begins to lose its human-like appearance, starting to look more like a monster or a living corpse. If my memory serves me right, the 1E Corebook even mentions needing makeup to cover-up &quot;corpse-like&quot; appearance as early as Humanity 4 or 5, hinting directly at the somewhat-obvious changes to the kindred's body. Some editions of Masquerade also mention those changes to kindred's physique.<br /> <br /> From that I can conclude that the general consensus across editions is that as Humanity descends, the Beast erodes not only the person's mind, but the body as well, twisting it into something... different. And yet, in Requiem (at least 2E) penalties for low Humanity do not include anything related to Social interactions, referring only to &quot;penalties on any roll to relate to humans&quot;. So, &quot;relate&quot;, but not actually interact with them. I understand that it's left kind-of open-ended on purpose, but I'd like to hear your thoughts on the matter of what rolls would actually be affected by this penalty.<br /> <br /> From what I see, the only skill that would absolutely fall under this penalty is Empathy, and even that is kind of questionable, as some of the actions that use Empathy are less about relating to humans and more about manipulating them. Sensing lies or fear, for example, is the classic ability of any ancient predator in fiction, so it doesn't make much sense to penalize it.<br /> <br /> Regarding the change in appearance, I always thought that exceptionally low Humanity (1 or 0) slowly turns kindred into those pale-skinned, featureless monsters (think Ancients from &quot;The Strain&quot;, Vampire-Angel from recent &quot;Midnight Mass&quot;, Petyr from &quot;What We Do in the Shadows&quot; or Count Orlok from original &quot;Nosferatu&quot;). But from what I see, degradation of the kindred's body to something moster-like is something reserved uniquely for Nosferatu clan, at least in in VtR 2e.<br /> <br /> So, I'm kind of asking for your opinion on that matter. Should low Humanity degrade kindred into monsters not just mentally but visually? Should it impose penalties to their social interaction with mortals? And if so, how to make Nosferatu fit into this without taking their clan's identity?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27533-vargock","name":"Vargock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T12:27:47-07:00","id":1492106,"title":"","content":"The humanity scale on page 106 of Vampire 2nd ed. rulebook gives an impression of the physical changes that appear in low Humanity Kindred. This starts at a Humanity score of 3 - Callous. The degeneration seems to be towards the corpse-like, exacerberated by the carelessness of the vampire towards its appearance. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","user":"Cabaal","date":". 09-01-2022, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T13:11:55-07:00","id":1492113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vargock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492104-some-thoughts-and-questions-about-low-humanity#post1492104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And yet, in Requiem (at least 2E) penalties for low Humanity do not include anything related to Social interactions, referring only to &quot;penalties on any roll to relate to humans&quot;. So, &quot;relate&quot;, but not actually interact with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what those are. The penalties basically apply to rolls to interact with humans in a relatable capacity instead of to hunt or exploit them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-01-2022, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T13:18:00-07:00","id":1492114,"title":"","content":"^It's hard to have a civil conversation with a person if you're shivering with gluttonous lust for their flesh. Low Humanity vampires don't realize that that's the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T05:05:36-07:00","id":1492152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492104-some-thoughts-and-questions-about-low-humanity?p=1492113#post1492113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what those are. The penalties basically apply to rolls to interact with humans in a relatable capacity instead of to hunt or exploit them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are you saying that the intention behind those rules was that those penalties affect <b>any </b>social rolls with humans that depend on relatability, not just your typical Empathy rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27533-vargock","name":"Vargock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T06:41:34-07:00","id":1492157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vargock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492104-some-thoughts-and-questions-about-low-humanity?p=1492152#post1492152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are you saying that the intention behind those rules was that those penalties affect <b>any </b>social rolls with humans that depend on relatability, not just your typical Empathy rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Well, any social roll that isn't in service to enacting predacity. Intimidation rolls will do just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T07:46:15-07:00","id":1492159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vargock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492104-some-thoughts-and-questions-about-low-humanity?p=1492152#post1492152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are you saying that the intention behind those rules was that those penalties affect <b>any </b>social rolls with humans that depend on relatability, not just your typical Empathy rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, if it's the type of interaction that would count for avoiding detachment rolls based on how long you've gone without human interaction, the penalty applies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T14:10:00-07:00","id":1492184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492104-some-thoughts-and-questions-about-low-humanity?p=1492157#post1492157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bingo.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Well, any social roll that isn't in service to enacting predacity. Intimidation rolls will do just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Well, it is good to hear that the penalties are not restricted just to Empathy, but gosh it is unclear from the text itself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27533-vargock","name":"Vargock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T15:11:06-07:00","id":1492186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vargock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492104-some-thoughts-and-questions-about-low-humanity?p=1492184#post1492184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Well, it is good to hear that the penalties are not restricted just to Empathy, but gosh it is unclear from the text itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's pretty plain, barring misreading:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Also, there are minor Social modifiers listed. These modifiers apply to </b><b>rolls relating to humans.</b> Manipulating humans for food with Subterfuge or frightening them with Intimidation are not affected; but trying to understand a human\u2019s emotional cues with the Empathy Skill would be affected. </div> </div> </div>Use of Empathy to understand people notwithstanding, a Social modifier affects Social rolls, which are defined in the section on Attributes as rolls that use a Social Attribute. The penalties are 2e's equivalent of 1e's Humanity-based cap on dicepools using Empathy, Persuasion, and Socialize against non-vampires.<br /> <br /> The penalty is specifically representative of a Kindred character's increasing inability to deal with humans outside the baseline context of being an undead predator who steals blood from people instead of as a fellow person participating in the (usually positive) experience of human community. It wouldn't talk about vampires having a hard time establishing relationships if the implication was just that you couldn't use one Social Skill as effectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T13:18:45-07:00","id":1492249,"title":"","content":"I think you may be mentally adding a word: it's not &quot;These modifiers apply to rolls<b> to relate</b> <b>to </b>humans&quot; as per the first post, it's &quot;rolls <b>relating to</b> humans.&quot; It's not relating as in &quot;empathizing&quot; (though that is the example that they give), it's relating as in &quot;having to do with.&quot; It's not the CHARACTERS relating to humans which is penalized, but the ROLLS which relate to humans that are penalized (though those rolls may be rolls to understand humans). <br /> <br /> They give two examples of exceptions to the general rule that Social rolls with humans are penalized, and one example of how that general rule plays out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}